WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Before you touch a single tool, you need to understand what HVAC systems
actually do.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
HVAC work involves serious hazards: high voltage (240V+), refrigerant exposure
(frostbite, asphyxiation in confined spaces), working at heights (rooftops,
ladders), hot surfaces (brazing, furnace heat exchangers), and rotating

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
LOTO: Lockout/Tagout — the procedure of disconnecting power, locking the
disconnect, and verifying 0 volts before working on equipment.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
PPE: Personal Protective Equipment — safety glasses, gloves, boots, hearing
protection, and respiratory protection as required by the task.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Arc Flash: An electrical explosion caused by a short circuit through air. Can
cause severe burns and death. Proper PPE and de-energization prevent arc flash
incidents.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Safety violations get you fired immediately.
No employer will tolerate a technician who skips LOTO or does not wear PPE. More
importantly, safety keeps you alive.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Watch out for these: ALWAYS verify 0 volts with YOUR OWN multimeter after
pulling the disconnect — never trust someone else. And — Refrigerant is heavier
than air — it sinks to the floor in enclosed spaces and displaces oxygen

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

